{"timestamp":"2026-10-02T10:46:20.340Z","ordinal":130,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0fc35-adc1-75f0-9dd2-992cdac53e53","turn_id":"01a0fc35-ae13-7531-a86c-c062b0ee4891","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_0b5fa48ff3662cca016abf8b75634087d28fd6173d95dabad2","summary_text":["**Processing line limits**\n\nI’m figuring out the limits of using `.readline()`, which allows reading one 10MB line at a time. The tool’s output can exceed 8MB, especially when dealing with large transcripts. To avoid failure, I need to skip oversized records by reading until a newline and updating the offset accordingly. If we encounter a huge user prompt, it’s crucial to provide an explicit status instead of making empty promises. Setting MAX_RECORD_BYTES to a central 16MiB seems better, but if there's unsupported data, it raises an error.","**Handling JSON and status errors**\n\nI'm navigating an issue with crashes that happen after appending data before the state stabilizes, particularly focusing on event IDs and their idempotent replay. If a malformed JSON occurs, it leads to a status error, preventing cursor advancement on the current record. One bad transcript doesn't block others, so I need to ensure error statuses are structured. I’m looking to capture essential status details while parsing Codex, preferring response items with designated content types, and ensuring that metadata is complete for the recording process.","**Managing recording completeness**\n\nI'm considering whether to avoid recording if the source is incomplete. If a user's message is truncated and marked as \"complete false,\" I need to handle this carefully, especially since I don't want to invent anything. I should check if the metadata indicates whether the source is complete. If not, I should reference the original material. In older schemas, there are potential duplicates, so I want to ensure I’m prioritizing correct response items and not risking any sensitive information from attachments.","**Managing user roles and iterations**\n\nI need to decide whether to exclude the `subagent_task` from the user role content. It seems that transcripts should remain separate to ensure accuracy. The root transcript should focus on agent messages, while the final child only binds when necessary. Updates from the main root can't be copied, and every iteration generates a commentary log. The user mentioned they want 100 variations, which means I need to implement a callback marker in the iteration pipeline. I have to clarify that I can't promise automatic captures for 100 variations unless triggered for each event."],"raw_content":[]},"started_at_ms":1790937973406,"completed_at_ms":1790937980339}}
